    dcterms:description "Red-team pass 2026-10-19 (Frankly_81). In Frankly_81, the same episode as the broadcast argument, Nate says 'education to the masses didn't work, isn't working, and won't work. However, education and inspiration of individuals does.' Daniel's TGS_31 premise is that an open society needs 'everybody' to do good sensemaking, and that if this is impossible the alternative is a small group made 'the new nobility'. Both diagnose the collapse of shared sensemaking, but Nate's response (educate the few) is close to the path Daniel names as the failure mode, so the two concepts diverge at the point of response. Drafted by Claude from the graph's episode records; awaiting MJSullivan's review."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.PowerSeekingAndComplicity_EducatingHyperAgents_Frankly_85 a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:confidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
