    thinkr:citesEpisode tgs:Monologue.Frankly_81_TimeTravelAndTheSuperorganism, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_85_TheLightTriad, tgs:Interview.TGS_126_AVisionForBetterment ;
    dcterms:description "Red-team pass 2026-10-19 (Frankly_85). In Frankly_85 Nate says 'traits will outcompete values in almost all circumstances.' Daniel's TGS_126 account says power competition selects dark-triad leaders who reshape the system to keep winning. Taken together, these cut against educating and inspiring hyper-agents to change their values (Frankly_81): a hyper-agent whose values widen would be outcompeted by one whose traits did not. Nate's own later view thus weakens the hope the bridge pairs with Daniel's account. Drafted by Claude from the graph's episode records; awaiting MJSullivan's review."@en ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date .

tgs:Evidence.MaximizingReturnsOnPower_MaximumPowerPrinciple_TGS_132 a thinkr:Evidence, owl:NamedIndividual ;
